W: 2. You take off the belly wool anf finikle out the crutch
W: Then you go up the neck, for the rules they are such,
W: You clean 'round the horns and the first shoulder down,
W: A long blow up the back and then you turn around.
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 3. And when the shearing's over and we've all got our check
W: We'll roll up our blueys and we're off on the track.
W: The first town we come to, well, there we'll have a spree,
W: And ev'ry one that comes along 'll join in with me.
W: (Refrain)
